<title>BELGIUM: Britain, France to get extra EU raw cane quotas.</title>
<headline>Britain, France to get extra EU raw cane quotas.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union's sugar management committee is expected to approve on Wednesday an additional quota of 33,000 tonnes of preferential raw cane sugar imports into Britain and France, EU officials said.</p>
<p>France would receive 18,000 tonnes and Britain 15,000 tonnes between March 1 and June 30 to make up for shortfalls in deliveries from French overseas departments and other suppliers.</p>
</text>
